I"�/<p>An L&amp;D team considering alternatives to Credly should define its award rules and recurring operations before comparing vendors. CertifyMe, Accredible and Sertifier all merit evaluation; programme size alone does not establish which one can handle your governance. This is CertifyMe’s blog, not an independently scored shortlist. Primary product sources were checked on 4 October 2026.</p>

<h2 id="scope-and-maturity-remain-the-useful-framework">Scope and maturity remain the useful framework</h2>

<p><strong>Scope</strong> describes what the programme must do: attendance awards, assessed milestones, recurring compliance refreshers or connected pathways. <strong>Maturity</strong> describes the team’s governance: approved criteria, authoritative employee data, integration ownership, exception handling and evidence retention. A small team may have complex obligations; a large team may run a simple workflow.</p>

<p>Ask who authorizes each award, what triggers expiry or renewal, what access departing employees retain and whether external verification is needed. Separate internal readiness decisions from publicly shared achievements.</p>

